@startuml reader
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide empty members
title Python Reader — domain, service and server

package "Core (no HTTP, no hardware)" {
  class ReaderCore {
    +reader_id: str
    +allow_new_devices: bool = True
    +allow_new_sensors: bool = True
    +on_observation: Callable(Observation)
    +add_device(device)
    +get_device(device_id)
    +remove_device(device_id)
    +create_observation(device_id, sensor_id, value, phenomenon_time)
    +ingest(observation, send=True): bool
    +send_observation(observation)
  }
  class Device {
    +device_id: str
    +device_type: str
    +platform: str
    +add_sensor(sensor)
    +get_sensor(sensor_id)
    +remove_sensor(sensor_id)
    +list_sensors()
  }
  class Sensor {
    +sensor_id: str
    +device_id: str
    +observable_property: str
    +procedure: str
    +feature_of_interest: str
    +unit: str
    +build_observation(raw_value, phenomenon_time)
  }
  class Observation {
    +observation_id: str
    +device_id: str
    +sensor_id: str
    +observable_property: str
    +simple_result: Any
    +phenomenon_time: datetime
    +feature_of_interest: str
    +procedure: str
    +unit: str
  }
}
package "Service and outputs" {
  class ReaderService {
    +ingest(observation): bool
    +publish(observation)
    +metadata(stream_enabled=False)
    +devices()
  }
  interface ObservationOutput {
    +publish(reader_id, observation)
  }
  class StreamOutput
  class ManagerOutput {
    +managers: tuple
    +timeout: float
    +publish(reader_id, observation)
  }
  class ObservationStream {
    +subscribe()
    +publish(event)
    +close()
  }
  class "JSON serialization" as JSON {
    +observation_to_dict(observation)
    +observation_event(reader_id, observation)
  }
}
package "Optional HTTP server" {
  class ReaderServer {
    +start()
    +stop()
    +status()
    +app
  }
  class ServerConfig {
    +enabled: bool = False
    +host: str = 127.0.0.1
    +port: int = 3002
    +token: str
    +stream_enabled: bool = True
    +queue_size: int = 256
  }
}
ReaderCore o-- "0..*" Device : local devices
Device o-- "0..*" Sensor
Sensor ..> Observation : builds
ReaderCore ..> Observation : validates and emits
ReaderService --> ReaderCore : uses an external core\nand installs its callbacks
ReaderService o-- "0..*" ObservationOutput : fans out observations
StreamOutput ..|> ObservationOutput
ManagerOutput ..|> ObservationOutput
StreamOutput --> JSON
ManagerOutput --> JSON
StreamOutput --> ObservationStream
ReaderServer *-- ReaderService : composes
ReaderServer --> ReaderCore : receives an external instance
ReaderServer --> ServerConfig
ReaderServer --> ObservationStream
ReaderServer ..> StreamOutput : added when the stream is enabled
note bottom of ReaderCore
  on_observation can be a user function.
  When ReaderService is attached, it owns the callbacks.
  The core never serializes or sends HTTP by itself.
end note
note bottom of ManagerOutput
  HTTP push: POST /newEvent to every configured
  Manager, with the token in the body.
end note
note bottom of ReaderServer
  GET /health, /metadata, /devices, /devices/{id}
  GET /stream (SSE, optional)
  GET /info and /logs without a token
  The C++ core and the ESP32 example
  follow the same event contract.
end note
@enduml
